  "task": "# Relay stage 1: Ideate\nTask: avoid-confusing-tasks-with-identical-names\nWorking directory: /Volumes/Tera/dev/visual-relay/\nProtected paths (queue bookkeeping \u2014 never part of this task's diff): llm-tasks/, .relay/, .relay-scratch/, .swival/\n\n## Task input\n# Avoid confusing tasks with identical names\n\nI created the \"speed-up-automated-tests\" task from a template again. It then showed all stages complete. This was likely because a task with the same name was already completed. I've since deleted the duplicate and created a new one with a unique name as a workaround.\n\nIt should be possible to create tasks with the same name later on and not have it confused with a completed task.\n\nCare should also be taken not to overwrite them. Up to you to decide how, but one idea would be to move completed tasks into a GUID subfolder on completion to avoid collisions.\n\n## Manifest\n(not set yet)\n\n## Prior stages\n\n\nEnd your reply with a single fenced ```json block, nothing after it, matching: { \"summary\": string, \"options\": string[] }",
